    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1089">

                <pb facs="1130" n="1120" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-14T18:00:00+08:00">July 14, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 14—10:58 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1525. Re Shanghai’s 2667, July 8 to Dept,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d1089-f1"/>
                    repeated EmbOff Canton 864. We concur with recommendation in Shanghai’s
                    reference telegram that we should make representations against Nationalist air
                    attacks on Shanghai and other large population centers not only because <pb
                        facs="1131" n="1121" xml:id="pg1121"/> of inflammation of anti-American
                    sentiment but also on humanitarian grounds and because of their doubtful
                    military utility in any case. We recall that representations to Chinese
                    Government last November re Nationalist bombing of Mukden seemed to have some
                    effect, though representations were limited to concern over American lives and
                    property Mukden.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1525, repeated Shanghai 856, EmbOff Canton 637.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
